#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_min_limit

#% text
# `discrete_min_limit(f, k -> inf)` gives the lower limit of the sequence f(k) as the integer k grows; `k -> -inf` as it decreases.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The method is that of `discrete_max_limit`, with the smallest of the limits along the residues.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
discrete_min_limit((-1)^k, k -> inf)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
discrete_min_limit((-1)^k*3*k^2/(k^2 + 5), k -> inf)
#% output
#= -3

#% cell
discrete_min_limit(cos(k), k -> inf)
#% output
#= -1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `discrete_max_limit`, `min_limit`
